      "explanation": "For WIDTH >= 7, including the default 128, this invariant holds after reset and is preserved by each transition. Initially x=y=0. Both increase together through x=y=49. Because assignments are blocking, the next transition increments x to 50 before updating y, producing y=48 and establishing x+y=98. Subsequent active transitions preserve this sum until x=99,y=-1. The invariant makes this the only active state with negative y, so setting flag to 1 necessarily leaves x=99 and decrements y to -2. Otherwise the next state remains active and satisfies the invariant. When flag>=1, all registers hold, preserving prop. Thus this lemma and prop together are 1-inductive."
